# Google Apps Script URL that backs the Station Portal backend.
# For local dev: copy this file to .env and fill in the value.
# For GitHub Pages: set it as a repository secret named VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions).
VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=

# The Firebase web config, for the move onto Firestore (see docs/FIRESTORE_MODEL.md). These are NOT secrets: a
# Firebase web config is public by design, and the project is protected by security rules and App Check. They are
# commented out until the app reads them, so the build is unaffected in the meantime. Values come from the Firebase
# console: Project settings > Your apps > Web app > SDK setup and configuration.
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# The FCM web-push certificate key, from Project settings > Cloud Messaging > Web configuration.
# VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=

# Which features read and write Firestore instead of Google Sheets, comma-separated: `memberPayload`, `availability`,
# `clock`, `offers`, `scheduleBoard`, `adminPayload`. Leave it unset and nothing is routed, which is the safe default -
# every build behaves exactly as it did before the move. A feature is only routed when Firebase is configured, its
# prerequisites are named too, and somebody is signed in to Firebase (see src/services/firestoreRouting.js).
# VITE_FIRESTORE_FEATURES=
